 34SI c  {+34}Mg produced through fragmentation of 1.4 GeV proton beam on a     
 34SI2c  UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN facility, selectively ionized using the   
 34SI3c  Resonance Ionization Laser Ion Source (RILIS) and selected by the      
 34SI4c  ISOLDE General Purpose Separator (GPS).  Nuclei were implanted on a    
 34SI5c  movable tape. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b|g, |g(t) using five HPGe     
 34SI6c  Clover detectors and a 3 cm thick NE102 plastic scintillator.          
